521
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:26,600
 Paul says this, right after we watchful,

522
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:29,660
 he says to stand firm in the faith,

523
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:30,880
 which gives you your second point.

524
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:33,240
 A man of God lives with conviction.

525
00:21:33,240 --> 00:21:36,800
 A man of God lives with conviction.

526
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:38,400
 Notice he doesn't say,

527
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:40,880
 you should stand firm in your personality,

528
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:42,640
 in your opinions, in your political position,

529
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:44,900
 in your personal preferences or your favorite team.

530
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:46,380
 Why?

531
00:21:46,380 --> 00:21:47,480
 Because here's the truth.

532
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:50,380
 You're not an American man before you're God's man.

533
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:55,000
 You're not a boss man before you're God's man.

534
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,520
 You're not a hunting or golfing

535
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:58,880
 or cross-fitting man before you're God's man.

536
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:00,920
 You're not a ladies man before you're God's man.

537
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:02,720
 You're not a man's man before you're God's man.

538
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:04,600
 You're not a family man before you're God's man.

539
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:08,000
 You're not a wing man before you're God's man,

540
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:09,680
 even though some of your boys need you to be one of those.

541
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:10,920
 So learn how to be a wing man

542
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:12,760
 'cause every brother is served well by somebody

543
00:22:12,760 --> 00:22:14,160
 that can step into that gap.

544
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:17,120
 None of these titles make you into a man.

545
00:22:17,120 --> 00:22:19,440
 Only God can do that.

546
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:23,000
 That's why we have to stand firm in our faith.

547
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:26,160
 Hebrews 11 says, "Now faith is the assurance of things

548
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:28,720
 "hoped for, the conviction of things not seen."

549
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:29,960
 What is conviction?

550
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:34,040
 Well, Hebrews 11 gives us a good idea.

551
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:36,720
 It says that a synonymous word,

552
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:39,640
 a parallel consideration would be assurance.

553
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:42,640
 You see, conviction is an unwavering belief

554
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:46,040
 in someone or something that cannot fail,

555
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:49,960
 which is the reason God is the only true source

556
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:53,680
 of conviction because God has been the only safe bet

557
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:54,760
 for all time.

558
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:58,320
 He has only always guaranteed his promises.

559
00:22:58,320 --> 00:23:01,000
 He is the only sure thing out there.

560
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,960
 So let me ask you, fellas,

561
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:05,760
 why is it then that so many guys struggle

562
00:23:05,760 --> 00:23:08,640
 to stand firm in Him?

563
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:13,700
 Because it is hard to stand firm

564
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:15,400
 in a faith you barely know.

565
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:21,960
 It is hard to stand firm in a faith that you barely know.

566
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:23,120
 Just think about it.

567
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:26,880
 Your confidence in something directly correlates

568
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:29,120
 to your knowledge of that something.

569
00:23:29,120 --> 00:23:31,320
 Some of you guys, you have an immense amount of confidence

570
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:35,040
 at the gym because you know what to do at the gym.

571
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:38,060
 Some of you, you have a lot of confidence with the ladies

572
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:41,720
 because you know they don't want you to play any games.

573
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:44,480
 They just want you to walk up and be normal for once.

574
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:47,960
 Some of you, you have an immense amount of confidence

575
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:49,480
 in your investments because you understand

576
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:50,880
 what's happening in the marketplace.

577
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:54,160
 Some of you, you have a lot of confidence in the cowboys.

578
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:56,040
 (congregation laughing)

579
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:58,600
 Even though we've been battered one too many times

580
00:23:58,600 --> 00:24:00,400
 to have such confidence.

581
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:03,560
 The level of your confidence depends directly

582
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:04,720
 on the level of your knowledge.

583
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:07,160
 And the reason you have such little confidence in God

584
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:11,080
 is because you have such little knowledge of God.

585
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:12,400
 You have such little confidence in Him

586
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:14,040
 because you have little knowledge of Him.

587
00:24:14,040 --> 00:24:15,960
 And because of this, here's the thing.

588
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:19,520
 So many of us, we will preach our problems to God

589
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:21,600
 as opposed to preach God to our problems.

590
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:24,960
 You need to know Him.

591
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:26,840
 So how do you do it?

592
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:28,160
 You read the Bible.

593
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:31,800
 Sophisticated answer, right?

594
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:33,060
 Like that's what you do.

595
00:24:33,060 --> 00:24:35,300
 You grab this book and you open it up.

596
00:24:35,300 --> 00:24:37,420
 You don't read it from your phone.

597
00:24:37,420 --> 00:24:40,800
 You get the book, you peel open the leather,

598
00:24:40,800 --> 00:24:44,240
 you read through the pages, you ask it good questions,

599
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:47,360
 you receive its questions and you consider them carefully.

600
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:49,960
 You don't outsource your theology to a podcast

601
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:52,120
 or to Instagram or to your girlfriend.

602
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:54,280
 You choose to do the work yourself.

603
00:24:54,280 --> 00:24:55,960
 If you feel confronted by a passage,

604
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:57,680
 you don't lean out, you lean in.

605
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:00,460
 And then you look up and you ask Him to give more.

606
00:25:00,460 --> 00:25:02,840
 Like this is the way that we should express

607
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:04,080
 our dependence on God.

608
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:06,400
 We come to learn about Him.

609
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,480
 We need to know this God.

610
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:12,640
 I pray like, yes, I want you to have a faith

611
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:14,640
 that is full of the experience of God,

612
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:16,240
 but do not have a faith that is empty

613
00:25:16,240 --> 00:25:18,560
 of the reason for God as well.

614
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:20,180
 You need both.

615
00:25:20,180 --> 00:25:22,360
 We're called to be true worshipers, which are what?

616
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:24,560
 In spirit and in truth.

617
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:28,160
 What's typically true is we major in one

618
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:30,000
 and we suck at the other one.

619
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:33,200
 No, be good at both.

620
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:37,080
 Like learn this book and then learn the spirit

621
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:39,760
 who illuminates your eyes to see within it.

622
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:42,440
 You have to know Him.

623
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:45,880
 And the reason why is 'cause that's what leads you

624
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:46,920
 to mature manhood.

625
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:48,640
 Ephesians 4, it tells us this.

626
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:50,880
 It says in verses 13 to 14,

627
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:52,760
 it says that God is building up the body.

628
00:25:52,760 --> 00:25:55,640
 He's given those in the church

629
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:58,400
 until we all attain to the unity of the faith

630
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:00,980
 and to the knowledge of the Son of God to mature manhood,

631
00:26:00,980 --> 00:26:03,540
 to the measure of the stature of the fullness of Christ,

632
00:26:03,540 --> 00:26:04,380
 which is important.

633
00:26:04,380 --> 00:26:05,600
 We gotta stop 'cause you need to understand

634
00:26:05,600 --> 00:26:08,320
 like He just told you what mature manhood looks like.

635
00:26:08,320 --> 00:26:09,280
 It looks like Jesus.

636
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:11,040
 You caught that, right?

637
00:26:11,040 --> 00:26:13,340
 Like mature manhood, it does not look like your physique.

638
00:26:13,340 --> 00:26:14,680
 It doesn't look like your beard.

639
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:15,920
 It doesn't look like your bank account.

640
00:26:15,920 --> 00:26:17,240
 It doesn't look like your body count.

641
00:26:17,240 --> 00:26:19,480
 It looks like Jesus Christ.

642
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:21,520
 That's what mature manhood is.

643
00:26:21,520 --> 00:26:22,360
 And He goes on.

644
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:23,960
 He says, "So that way we may no longer be children

645
00:26:23,960 --> 00:26:25,220
 "tossed to and fro by the waves

646
00:26:25,220 --> 00:26:26,940
 "and carried about by every wind of doctrine,

647
00:26:26,940 --> 00:26:30,640
 "by human cunning, by craftiness in deceitful schemes."

648
00:26:30,640 --> 00:26:33,760
 Translation, your confidence in God increases

649
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:36,040
 when your confidence in God increases,

650
00:26:36,040 --> 00:26:38,280
 your confidence in life increases.

651
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:39,900
 That's what he's saying.

652
00:26:39,900 --> 00:26:41,520
 Why is that?

653
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:44,860
 Because you know His plans can't be stopped.

654
00:26:44,860 --> 00:26:46,440
 His purposes, they can't be thwarted.

655
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:48,260
 His people cannot be taken.

656
00:26:48,260 --> 00:26:49,920
 And when you know that about God,

657
00:26:49,920 --> 00:26:52,720
 that He actually does reign over it all,

658
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:56,240
 He is actually supreme over everything.

659
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:59,060
 He holds all things together by the word of His power.

660
00:26:59,060 --> 00:27:01,160
 When you know that is your God,

661
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:04,560
 it changes the way you move through the world.

662
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:07,560
 Like, it gives you a different sort of swagger.

663
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:10,680
 Not the weird machismo, silly kind that you see

664
00:27:10,680 --> 00:27:11,520
 where dating coaches are like,

665
00:27:11,520 --> 00:27:13,000
 "You gotta do the shoulder sway."

666
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,280
 Not that kind of swagger.

667
00:27:14,280 --> 00:27:16,160
 It gives you a swagger that is sure,

668
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:18,480
 and it's steady, and it's certain.

669
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:22,120
 Because you know a God that is sure, and steady, and certain

670
00:27:22,120 --> 00:27:23,360
 and because He is that way,

671
00:27:23,360 --> 00:27:27,320
 you have confidence that you can move through life likewise.

672
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:30,720
 And when you have that sort of demeanor,

673
00:27:30,720 --> 00:27:31,840
 it's the kind of confidence

674
00:27:31,840 --> 00:27:35,280
 that dignifies people's confidence in you.

675
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:38,240
 Like, it helps you to be a man of your word

676
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:39,880
 so you can keep it whenever you give it.

677
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:43,240
 It's the kind of confidence that makes difficult decisions

678
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:44,600
 when other people cannot do it.

679
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:46,960
 It's the kind of confidence that it stays the course

680
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:50,160
 even when difficult days come and trials abound.

681
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:52,520
 It's the kind of confidence that inspires a woman

682
00:27:52,520 --> 00:27:55,760
 to walk with you for a child to look up to you

683
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:58,440
 and a family to be led by you.

684
00:27:58,440 --> 00:28:00,120
 This is what you need.

685
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:04,880
 You need to have a faith upon which you can stand, burn.

686
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:06,820
 So many men are tossed about

687
00:28:06,820 --> 00:28:10,800
 because they don't have a solid rock upon which to stand.

688
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:14,200
 Christ has come that you might have something so solid.

689
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:17,600
 So why don't you stand on Him?

690
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:23,400
 And if you know Him, and it feels shaky nonetheless,

691
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:25,500
 you do not know Him as well as you should.

692
00:28:26,760 --> 00:28:31,760
 The good news is you that seek to know Him more

693
00:28:31,760 --> 00:28:33,960
 can have the confidence that He sought

694
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:36,400
 to be known by you first.

695
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:38,040
 That's how good your King is.

696
00:28:38,040 --> 00:28:41,560
 A man of God lives with conviction

697
00:28:41,560 --> 00:28:46,760
 because, and this is important, Jesus died with conviction.

698
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:51,440
 He knew full well the plans that God had to save His people,

699
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:54,120
 the price that Christ Himself would have to pay to do it,

700
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:57,000
 and the cost that a relationship with us would require,

701
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,600
 and He went to the cross anyways.

702
00:28:58,600 --> 00:29:00,680
 He has shown us what conviction looks like,

703
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:01,840
 and He has filled us with the Spirit

704
00:29:01,840 --> 00:29:04,280
 so that by His strength and not our own,

705
00:29:04,280 --> 00:29:05,320
 we can live the same.

706
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:12,680
 The next point we catch whenever Paul says to act like men.

707
00:29:12,680 --> 00:29:16,520
 This point is that a man of God acts courageously.

708
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:18,600
 A man of God acts courageously

709
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:23,280
 because courage is what moves a man from point one and two

710
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:25,200
 into the rest of the points in this passage.

711
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:26,560
 That's the beauty of it.

712
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:30,600
 Like what moves a man of watchfulness and truthfulness

713
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:32,580
 into action is courage.

714
00:29:32,580 --> 00:29:37,100
 I love the way that God commissions Joshua in Joshua 1.

715
00:29:37,100 --> 00:29:41,600
 He says this, He says, "Be strong and courageous."

716
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:44,080
 That's the same word in the Septuagint.

717
00:29:44,080 --> 00:29:46,200
 "For you shall cause this people to inherit the land

718
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:47,920
 "that I swore to their fathers to give them.

719
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:50,480
 "Only be strong and very courageous,

720
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:52,120
 "being careful to do according to all the law

721
00:29:52,120 --> 00:29:53,320
 "that most of my servant commanded you.

722
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:55,400
 "Do not turn from it to the right hand or the left,

723
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:57,600
 "that you may have good success wherever you go."

724
00:29:57,600 --> 00:29:59,360
 And then verse nine, "Have I not commanded you,

725
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:01,080
 "be strong and courageous?"

726
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:02,200
 Yeah, God, we got it.

727
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:03,340
 You said it a few times.

728
00:30:03,340 --> 00:30:05,080
 "Don't be frightened, don't be dismayed,

729
00:30:05,080 --> 00:30:07,700
 "for the Lord your God is with you wherever you go."

730
00:30:07,700 --> 00:30:09,840
 You see, here's the thing, fellas, look at me.

731
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:12,660
 Any guy can have the best of intention,

732
00:30:12,660 --> 00:30:17,920
 but it takes a real man to follow through with action.

733
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:22,360
 Like, I see it every, every single Tuesday night.

734
00:30:22,360 --> 00:30:24,380
 Like, some girl will come down

735
00:30:24,380 --> 00:30:26,440
 and will talk to me about her relationship,

736
00:30:26,440 --> 00:30:27,800
 and she'll say something like this.

737
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:30,000
 Like, "He knows that he's supposed to pursue me more,

738
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:31,480
 "and he's told me that he wants to do that."

739
00:30:31,480 --> 00:30:34,040
 Or, "He knows that we're supposed to have purity

740
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:35,800
 "in our relationship, and so he wants to do a better job

741
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:37,360
 "of honoring our parameters."

742
00:30:37,360 --> 00:30:40,240
 Or, "He knows that he shouldn't speak to me that way,

743
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:41,360
 "and he's told me that he wants to do better,

744
00:30:41,360 --> 00:30:42,560
 "and he wants to try harder."

745
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:45,720
 And every single time I talk to these ladies,

746
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:49,000
 I just feel something in my heart hurt so deeply for them,

747
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:50,640
 because I think about my own daughter

748
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:52,280
 who is coming into the world soon,

749
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:53,600
 and I just want her to know,

750
00:30:53,600 --> 00:30:55,120
 as well as every woman here to know,

751
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:57,840
 by way of you men, that a man of God

752
00:30:57,840 --> 00:31:00,400
 doesn't need to be defended by a woman,

753
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:02,560
 because he does the work of defending.

754
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:05,280
 You tracking?

755
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:07,600
 Like, men of God do not need someone

756
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:10,200
 to make excuses for them.

757
00:31:10,200 --> 00:31:14,800
 Men of God make efforts for those people instead.

758
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:18,240
 Because he's courageous.

759
00:31:18,240 --> 00:31:20,680
 Like, literally, that's what the word here means.

760
00:31:20,680 --> 00:31:22,080
 When he says, "Act like men,"

761
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:26,680
 that word actually means to prove yourself to be a man,

762
00:31:26,680 --> 00:31:30,760
 to be brave, to be mature, to be self-controlled,

763
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:33,160
 all of which does not come by way of your own strength.

764
00:31:33,160 --> 00:31:36,520
 It comes by way of the Spirit at work within you.

765
00:31:36,520 --> 00:31:40,400
 But here's the thing.

766
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:42,040
 A boy didn't know how to do that.

767
00:31:44,240 --> 00:31:49,240
 My son is a boy, and I love him to death.

768
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:56,760
 He is cute, and he is fun,

769
00:31:56,760 --> 00:31:58,600
 and he will melt your heart

770
00:31:58,600 --> 00:32:00,880
 if he falls in and snuggles with you.

771
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:08,320
 But at the same time, he will smack you in the face,

772
00:32:08,320 --> 00:32:12,320
 throw food at you, and scream until he gets his way.

773
00:32:12,320 --> 00:32:13,280
 Why does he do that?

774
00:32:13,280 --> 00:32:15,680
 How can these two things exist at the same time?

775
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:17,260
 Because he's immature.

776
00:32:17,260 --> 00:32:21,040
 The difference between my boy and your boy

777
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:23,840
 is my boy's two and your boy's like 30.

778
00:32:23,840 --> 00:32:25,200
 That's the difference here.

779
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:27,520
 And the truth of the matter is,

