00:42:57,800 --> 00:43:01,200
 I'm in conflict all the time.

1040
00:43:01,200 --> 00:43:04,720
 At work, at home, with friends.

1041
00:43:04,720 --> 00:43:06,920
 I'm a passionate guy.

1042
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:09,560
 It's hard to reign this in sometimes.

1043
00:43:09,560 --> 00:43:12,740
 I understand you might be in conflict with someone.

1044
00:43:14,160 --> 00:43:16,720
 You might be in conflict with your girl.

1045
00:43:16,720 --> 00:43:17,560
 That's hard.

1046
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:18,480
 She's smarter than you.

1047
00:43:18,480 --> 00:43:21,280
 She's probably more right than you are,

1048
00:43:21,280 --> 00:43:22,680
 and you're gonna have to swallow your pride,

1049
00:43:22,680 --> 00:43:24,960
 and that's gonna be a tough pill to take.

1050
00:43:24,960 --> 00:43:27,760
 But godly men, they persist through the pain

1051
00:43:27,760 --> 00:43:30,760
 because they know the outcome is worth it on the other side.

1052
00:43:30,760 --> 00:43:32,920
 You got godly strength,

1053
00:43:32,920 --> 00:43:34,960
 then you can stop choosing the path of least resistance.

1054
00:43:34,960 --> 00:43:36,440
 I'll give you one sound bite on this.

1055
00:43:36,440 --> 00:43:37,440
 The path of greatest faith

1056
00:43:37,440 --> 00:43:39,680
 is never the path of least resistance.

1057
00:43:39,680 --> 00:43:40,840
 You choosing the easy way out?

1058
00:43:40,840 --> 00:43:41,840
 Jesus didn't do that.

1059
00:43:41,840 --> 00:43:42,960
 Praise God he didn't.

1060
00:43:44,480 --> 00:43:46,040
 You can stop self-indulging

1061
00:43:46,040 --> 00:43:48,760
 because comfort isn't the goal, God's glory is.

1062
00:43:48,760 --> 00:43:51,360
 It's impossible to truly serve someone and stay comfortable

1063
00:43:51,360 --> 00:43:53,480
 unless the person you're trying to serve is yourself.

1064
00:43:53,480 --> 00:43:54,880
 You ever thought about that?

1065
00:43:54,880 --> 00:43:57,840
 Like men, listen to me.

1066
00:43:57,840 --> 00:44:00,980
 You push the snooze, that serves you.

1067
00:44:00,980 --> 00:44:02,360
 You're on your phone when you're with your friends,

1068
00:44:02,360 --> 00:44:03,180
 that serves you.

1069
00:44:03,180 --> 00:44:05,640
 You call in instead of drive in for that meeting,

1070
00:44:05,640 --> 00:44:06,480
 that serves you.

1071
00:44:06,480 --> 00:44:07,520
 It doesn't serve anybody else.

1072
00:44:07,520 --> 00:44:10,320
 You objectify that girl by fantasizing over her photos

1073
00:44:10,320 --> 00:44:12,120
 when she's not, that serves you.

1074
00:44:12,120 --> 00:44:14,680
 You video game to save a fantasy world

1075
00:44:14,680 --> 00:44:16,560
 while the real world is burning down around you,

1076
00:44:16,560 --> 00:44:18,160
 that serves you.

1077
00:44:18,160 --> 00:44:19,800
 We do not serve ourselves.

1078
00:44:19,800 --> 00:44:22,680
 Men of God, we seek to serve others.

1079
00:44:22,680 --> 00:44:23,520
 Why?

1080
00:44:23,520 --> 00:44:24,560
 Because Christ has served us

1081
00:44:24,560 --> 00:44:26,280
 in that he gave his life for us.

1082
00:44:26,280 --> 00:44:27,800
 So give your life away.

1083
00:44:27,800 --> 00:44:29,560
 And then the last one is

1084
00:44:29,560 --> 00:44:31,360
 you can stop abdicating responsibility.

1085
00:44:31,360 --> 00:44:35,040
 Like why do guys blame other people for their problems?

1086
00:44:35,040 --> 00:44:37,640
 Adam did it with Eve, Abraham did it with Sarah,

1087
00:44:37,640 --> 00:44:39,560
 Aaron did it with the Israelites and the golden calf.

1088
00:44:39,560 --> 00:44:40,400
 We do it today.

1089
00:44:40,400 --> 00:44:41,340
 Why does this happen?

1090
00:44:43,120 --> 00:44:45,000
 Because we're fragile.

1091
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:48,280
 It's the truth.

1092
00:44:48,280 --> 00:44:52,200
 Like we may look all tough and rough on the outside,

1093
00:44:52,200 --> 00:44:57,120
 but on the inside, many, many men are wildly insecure.

1094
00:44:57,120 --> 00:45:01,040
 But godly men, they see broken and busted situations

1095
00:45:01,040 --> 00:45:02,360
 and instead of making excuses

1096
00:45:02,360 --> 00:45:03,200
 and letting someone else do it,

1097
00:45:03,200 --> 00:45:05,240
 they step in and they say, "I'll handle it."

1098
00:45:05,240 --> 00:45:06,240
 And that's what Jesus did.

1099
00:45:06,240 --> 00:45:07,800
 That's what we do.

1100
00:45:07,800 --> 00:45:10,960
 God is making miracles out of men

1101
00:45:10,960 --> 00:45:12,040
 who rely not on their strength,

1102
00:45:12,040 --> 00:45:12,920
 I love what Philip Brooks says.

1103
00:45:12,920 --> 00:45:14,880
 He says, "Do not pray for easy lives.

1104
00:45:14,880 --> 00:45:17,000
 "Pray for stronger men.

1105
00:45:17,000 --> 00:45:18,980
 "Don't pray for tasks equal to your powers.

1106
00:45:18,980 --> 00:45:22,240
 "Pray for powers equal to your tasks.

1107
00:45:22,240 --> 00:45:24,520
 "Then the doing of your work shall be no miracle,

1108
00:45:24,520 --> 00:45:27,260
 "but you, you shall be the miracle."

1109
00:45:27,260 --> 00:45:31,520
 He's wanting to make a miracle out of you, fellas.

1110
00:45:31,520 --> 00:45:32,520
 You want to let him?

1111
00:45:32,520 --> 00:45:34,880
 Last point.

1112
00:45:34,880 --> 00:45:36,640
 Man of God does everything in love.

1113
00:45:36,640 --> 00:45:39,840
 Man of God does everything with love.

1114
00:45:39,840 --> 00:45:41,360
 That's what Paul says in verse 14,

1115
00:45:41,360 --> 00:45:42,720
 which is an interesting end to this, right?

1116
00:45:42,720 --> 00:45:44,760
 Like he's just rolled out the tape for all the men.

1117
00:45:44,760 --> 00:45:47,020
 He's like, "Hey, you be watchful, you stand firm,

1118
00:45:47,020 --> 00:45:50,440
 "you act like a man, you be courageous, you be strong,

1119
00:45:50,440 --> 00:45:51,600
 "and you do everything in love,"

1120
00:45:51,600 --> 00:45:53,680
 which just feels like a really strange place

1121
00:45:53,680 --> 00:45:54,920
 to land the plane.

1122
00:45:54,920 --> 00:45:57,280
 And yet when you think about what true manhood is

1123
00:45:57,280 --> 00:46:00,560
 and who the true man is, it makes perfect sense.

1124
00:46:00,560 --> 00:46:01,400
 Why?

1125
00:46:01,400 --> 00:46:02,560
 Because God is love.

1126
00:46:02,560 --> 00:46:04,780
 Christ is the embodiment of God.

1127
00:46:04,780 --> 00:46:07,360
 And what we know by way of Christ is he was and he is,

1128
00:46:07,360 --> 00:46:09,000
 and he will always be love itself.

1129
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:11,800
 If your goal is to be like Christ, guess what?

1130
00:46:11,800 --> 00:46:14,560
 Love's on the horizon, fellas.

1131
00:46:14,560 --> 00:46:15,760
 That's what's happening to you.

1132
00:46:15,760 --> 00:46:18,120
 That's what will be true of you.

1133
00:46:18,120 --> 00:46:19,520
 First John four, it says this.

1134
00:46:19,520 --> 00:46:21,540
 It says, "Beloved, let us love one another,

1135
00:46:21,540 --> 00:46:22,540
 "for love is from God.

1136
00:46:22,540 --> 00:46:25,260
 "Whoever loves has been born of God, and he knows God.

1137
00:46:25,260 --> 00:46:26,980
 "Anyone who does not love," guess what?

1138
00:46:26,980 --> 00:46:29,840
 Doesn't know God because God is love.

1139
00:46:29,840 --> 00:46:30,720
 Verse nine.

1140
00:46:30,720 --> 00:46:32,920
 "In this, the love of God was made manifest among us."

1141
00:46:32,920 --> 00:46:33,760
 How?

1142
00:46:33,760 --> 00:46:35,240
 "He sent his only son into the world

1143
00:46:35,240 --> 00:46:36,660
 "so that we might live through him."

1144
00:46:36,660 --> 00:46:39,520
 Jump down to verse 19, "We love."

1145
00:46:39,520 --> 00:46:45,400
 We gotta do better on that.

1146
00:46:45,400 --> 00:46:48,400
 "We love because he first loved us."

1147
00:46:48,400 --> 00:46:52,400
 Verse 19, it is easily one of the most quotable scriptures

1148
00:46:52,400 --> 00:46:54,600
 in all the Bible, and here's the thing.

1149
00:46:54,600 --> 00:46:58,400
 Despite its familiarity for many of us, men most of all,

1150
00:46:58,400 --> 00:47:01,160
 the power of its truth has fallen on deaf ears.

1151
00:47:01,160 --> 00:47:02,800
 Why is that the case?

1152
00:47:02,800 --> 00:47:04,480
 I'll tell you why.

1153
00:47:04,480 --> 00:47:06,840
 It's because you think that this is kind of what God does.

1154
00:47:06,840 --> 00:47:08,240
 It sounds like work of the big guy, man.

1155
00:47:08,240 --> 00:47:09,840
 Like he just kind of loves everybody.

1156
00:47:09,840 --> 00:47:12,620
 No, the love of God has fallen on deaf ears.

1157
00:47:12,620 --> 00:47:14,600
 It has fallen on vacant hearts

1158
00:47:14,600 --> 00:47:18,820
 because we don't have a misunderstanding about who God is.

1159
00:47:18,820 --> 00:47:21,720
 We have a misunderstanding about who we are

1160
00:47:21,720 --> 00:47:25,640
 and the kind of love it would take to do what Christ has done.

1161
00:47:25,640 --> 00:47:28,640
 We fail to realize how far he would go to get to you,

1162
00:47:28,640 --> 00:47:32,080
 how much he would give to get you.

1163
00:47:32,080 --> 00:47:33,640
 We fail to realize how hard it would be

1164
00:47:33,640 --> 00:47:37,200
 for any one of us to do the same, and yet he did it.

1165
00:47:37,200 --> 00:47:38,020
 How did he do it?

1166
00:47:38,020 --> 00:47:41,520
 Not by accident, not by mistake, by choice.

1167
00:47:41,520 --> 00:47:44,440
 I look at every couple I've performed the weddings of

1168
00:47:44,440 --> 00:47:46,040
 and I stand in the altar, I tell them,

1169
00:47:46,040 --> 00:47:47,120
 "Love is sometimes a feeling."

1170
00:47:47,120 --> 00:47:49,480
 It's always a choice, it's always a choice.

1171
00:47:49,480 --> 00:47:50,300
 Why?

1172
00:47:50,300 --> 00:47:52,960
 There's no more incompatible couple in the world

1173
00:47:52,960 --> 00:47:54,400
 than Christ and his church.

1174
00:47:54,400 --> 00:47:57,280
 So why the heck does that relationship work?

1175
00:47:57,280 --> 00:48:01,920
 Because he chooses her again and again and again and again.

1176
00:48:01,920 --> 00:48:04,220
 Loves her sacrificially.

1177
00:48:04,220 --> 00:48:06,160
 The same should be true for us, fellas.

1178
00:48:06,160 --> 00:48:10,720
 See, it's interesting in the world,

1179
00:48:10,720 --> 00:48:13,440
 the world, it needs a reason to love you.

1180
00:48:13,440 --> 00:48:19,680
 But with God, God has given you a reason to love us instead.

1181
00:48:19,680 --> 00:48:20,520
 That crazy?

1182
00:48:20,520 --> 00:48:24,960
 Totally shifts the paradigm, flips it all on its head.

1183
00:48:24,960 --> 00:48:26,640
 And true men, God's men, they love

1184
00:48:26,640 --> 00:48:28,640
 because they have been loved themselves.

1185
00:48:28,640 --> 00:48:31,760
 We see needs and we move towards it.

1186
00:48:31,760 --> 00:48:33,400
 We see the hurting, we work to heal it.

1187
00:48:33,400 --> 00:48:35,080
 We see the crying, we seek to comfort it.

1188
00:48:35,080 --> 00:48:36,640
 We see the battle, we seek to fight it.

1189
00:48:36,640 --> 00:48:37,540
 That's what we do.

1190
00:48:37,540 --> 00:48:41,740
 It's the most loving thing you can do.

1191
00:48:41,740 --> 00:48:45,760
 And we do it all because he did it for us.

1192
00:48:45,760 --> 00:48:46,600
 Final story.

1193
00:48:46,600 --> 00:48:54,040
 Years ago, I had a young man that I was discipling.

1194
00:48:54,040 --> 00:48:55,480
 He had come into our ministry

1195
00:48:55,480 --> 00:49:01,120
 and he had recommitted his life to Christ

1196
00:49:01,120 --> 00:49:04,120
 because he had made an absolute mess of his life beforehand.

1197
00:49:04,120 --> 00:49:06,220
 And we were sitting over dinner

1198
00:49:06,220 --> 00:49:10,800
 and we were just processing the mess that he had made.

1199
00:49:10,800 --> 00:49:12,360
 Definitively, it was on him.

1200
00:49:12,360 --> 00:49:16,440
 And he was like, "What do I do with this?

1201
00:49:16,440 --> 00:49:19,780
 "I see the God, man.

1202
00:49:19,780 --> 00:49:23,660
 "I see Christ Jesus and I wanna be like that,

1203
00:49:23,660 --> 00:49:25,560
 "but I feel like in light of everything I've done,

1204
00:49:25,560 --> 00:49:27,160
 "that is so far off the grid.

1205
00:49:27,160 --> 00:49:28,620
 "It is impossible for me to reach.

1206
00:49:28,620 --> 00:49:30,320
 "How do I get there?

1207
00:49:30,320 --> 00:49:32,360
 "How do I be better than I've been?

1208
00:49:32,360 --> 00:49:35,040
 "How do I make right what all I've done wrong?

1209
00:49:35,040 --> 00:49:36,420
 "How do I move forward different

1210
00:49:36,420 --> 00:49:38,320
 "than the way I've moved in the past?"

1211
00:49:38,320 --> 00:49:45,720
 And I told him, I was like, "Man, you can't do any of it.

1212
00:49:45,720 --> 00:49:51,820
 "It is only by God and his grace that you come to life.

1213
00:49:51,820 --> 00:49:55,760
 "And it is only by God and his grace

1214
00:49:55,760 --> 00:49:58,160
 "that you move into the abundant life.

1215
00:50:00,020 --> 00:50:02,480
 "But on the other side of your salvation,

1216
00:50:02,480 --> 00:50:04,540
 "the way this works itself out,

1217
00:50:04,540 --> 00:50:08,480
 "to become a man of God,

1218
00:50:08,480 --> 00:50:11,960
 "you do it by his strength

1219
00:50:11,960 --> 00:50:17,980
 "and you do it through your choice."

1220
00:50:17,980 --> 00:50:23,140
 Every day, making the hard decision

1221
00:50:23,140 --> 00:50:26,960
 to walk the narrow road instead of the wide path.

1222
00:50:27,920 --> 00:50:31,080
 Every day, willing to swallow your pride

1223
00:50:31,080 --> 00:50:32,140
 for the benefit of other people.

1224
00:50:32,140 --> 00:50:35,620
 Every day, willing to live out

1225
00:50:35,620 --> 00:50:38,360
 what has been loved in every day.

1226
00:50:38,360 --> 00:50:41,880
 Making the choice to move with him

1227
00:50:41,880 --> 00:50:43,480
 in the way that he moved.

1228
00:50:43,480 --> 00:50:46,720
 It looks like being watchful

1229
00:50:46,720 --> 00:50:48,800
 because when we were not on guard,

1230
00:50:48,800 --> 00:50:51,040
 Christ was on guard for us.

1231
00:50:51,040 --> 00:50:53,560
 Lived perfectly where we could not.

1232
00:50:53,560 --> 00:50:55,480
 It looks like standing firm in the faith,

1233
00:50:55,480 --> 00:50:59,000
 acting, living with conviction

1234
00:50:59,000 --> 00:51:01,760
 because Christ had such conviction.

1235
00:51:01,760 --> 00:51:04,640
 He never once wavered or second-guessed

1236
00:51:04,640 --> 00:51:05,800
 what he was here to do.

1237
00:51:05,800 --> 00:51:11,800
 It looks like acting like a man,

1238
00:51:11,800 --> 00:51:15,040
 moving into maturity,

1239
00:51:15,040 --> 00:51:19,320
 taking up courage in doing what must be done

1240
00:51:19,320 --> 00:51:21,560
 because Christ did what must be done

1241
00:51:21,560 --> 00:51:24,280
 and how much courage did it take to go to the cross.

1242
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:29,960
 It looks like strength or resolve

1243
00:51:29,960 --> 00:51:31,960
 to persist when others would give way.

1244
00:51:31,960 --> 00:51:32,960
 Why?

1245
00:51:32,960 --> 00:51:35,840
 Because your beloved is worth it.

1246
00:51:35,840 --> 00:51:41,320
 And it looks like love, doing everything in love

1247
00:51:41,320 --> 00:51:47,440
 because Christ did everything like that himself.

1248
00:51:47,440 --> 00:51:54,000
 And the beauty of that guy's story

1249
00:51:54,000 --> 00:51:56,360
 in a moment when he felt like such a boy

1250
00:51:56,360 --> 00:52:00,280
 and there's just a couple of years along the way,

1251
00:52:00,280 --> 00:52:04,800
 having watched him do all that I just said,

1252
00:52:04,800 --> 00:52:08,240
 take the hard right over the easy wrong

1253
00:52:08,240 --> 00:52:09,720
 again and again and again.

1254
00:52:09,720 --> 00:52:15,760
 I stood in the altar with he and his wife

1255
00:52:15,760 --> 00:52:17,360
 on the day in which they were wed

1256
00:52:17,360 --> 00:52:22,000
 and I've never been more proud of someone.

1257
00:52:24,320 --> 00:52:25,680
 Not because he did it,

1258
00:52:25,680 --> 00:52:28,800
 because Christ did it.

1259
00:52:28,800 --> 00:52:33,920
 And he just agreed day after day,

1260
00:52:33,920 --> 00:52:35,960
 oh God, won't you do it again?

1261
00:52:35,960 --> 00:52:39,680
 It's by his strength.

1262
00:52:39,680 --> 00:52:41,360
 It is by your choice, gentlemen.

1263
00:52:41,360 --> 00:52:48,680
 Will you make the choice starting tonight?

1264
00:52:48,680 --> 00:52:53,200
 Let me pray you would.

1265
00:52:54,120 --> 00:52:55,040
 Lord, we love you.

1266
00:52:55,040 --> 00:53:05,400
 God, I want for these guys, what I want for my own son,

1267
00:53:05,400 --> 00:53:09,680
 what I pray over my boy every night.

1268
00:53:09,680 --> 00:53:15,000
 I want them, God, to be filled with wisdom.

1269
00:53:15,000 --> 00:53:17,800
 I want them, God, to be filled with courage.

1270
00:53:17,800 --> 00:53:20,160
 I want them, God, to know your truth.

1271
00:53:20,160 --> 00:53:23,360
 I want them, God, to be filled with compassion.

1272
00:53:24,720 --> 00:53:26,720
 I want them, God, to have your strength.

1273
00:53:26,720 --> 00:53:32,400
 Come, oh Lord, do it here.

1274
00:53:32,400 --> 00:53:36,080
 Do it now and do it with them, I pray.

1275
00:53:36,080 --> 00:53:42,680
 Christ be magnified in the way we move into this response.

1276
00:53:42,680 --> 00:53:48,240
 And may every choice the men make here

1277
00:53:48,240 --> 00:53:50,560
 roll up to the glory of God.

1278
00:53:50,560 --> 00:53:52,680
 And may it be for our world's good,

1279
00:53:54,160 --> 00:53:57,200
 and would it make us as men so very glad.

1280
00:53:57,200 --> 00:54:00,520
 We love you, Lord, and it is in your name

1281
00:54:00,520 --> 00:54:02,360
 we pray these things, amen.

